<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_SumpTarBeastGenStep.xml   UtinniPatches — SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S3 build pass

  GenStepDef for RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces (already built,
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces.cs —
  NOT rebuilt this pass, per this item's own scope), placing RUT_BeastBulge
  via the shared Miasma-built RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker element. A
  GenStepDef on its own runs on no map; registration is the separate
  Patches/RUT_SumpTarBeastGenStep_Register.xml (same split this folder's own
  precedent uses, e.g. RUT_Miasma_GradientAxisGenStep.xml /
  RUT_Miasma_GradientAxis_Register.xml, both read before writing this).

  Site validator: entirely stock Verse.ScattererValidator_TerrainDef
  (terrainDef=RM_TarDeep, radius=2 — "deep-tar regions," not a single cell).
  RM_TarDeep only generates within the Sump biome, so this validator is ALSO
  this GenStepDef's biome gate — same pattern RM_GenStep_GradientAxis's own
  header already documents for this mod ("registering it globally is safe
  for every OTHER biome too... only ever repaints... when the map's biome
  carries [the relevant extension]"). warnOnFail is false below because "no
  deep tar on this biome" is the expected case on every non-Sump map, not an
  exceptional one.

  "Far from map edge" is ALSO stock — GenStep_Scatterer's own
  minEdgeDistPct field (Verse/GenStep_Scatterer.cs, verified); no new
  validator class needed for either half of the spec's placement ask.

  count: the spec's own "N dormant beasts (INVENTED: 1-2)" ships here as a
  fixed 1 — GenStep_Scatterer has no IntRange count field (only a fixed int
  or a density-based countPer10kCellsRange), and "1-2" is itself INVENTED
  tuning the spec names no mechanism for; collapsing to a deterministic 1 is
  this pass's own simplification, not a silent drop — widening to a density
  range is a one-line change later, flagged in the item file.

  order 780: after vanilla terrain/mutator gen (210/220, per this mod's own
  M1 precedent) and the generic ScatterRuinsSimple (750, read via RimSage
  this pass), ahead of the heavier AncientJunkClusters (960, also read via
  RimSage) — deep-tar terrain must already exist on the map before this
  step's own validator can find it.

  MayRequire is load-bearing on the def's own tag: genStep Class and the one
  elements entry's Class both live in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.

  DEPLOY_HOLD'd together with RUT_BeastBulge.xml and this file's own
  Register patch (src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt) — RUT_BeastBulge has no art yet.
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_GenStep_TarBeastPlacement</defName>
    <order>780</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces">
      <count>1</count>
      <minEdgeDistPct>0.15</minEdgeDistPct>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
      <validators>
        <li Class="Verse.ScattererValidator_TerrainDef">
          <terrainDef>RM_TarDeep</terrainDef>
          <radius>2</radius>
        </li>
      </validators>
      <elements>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker">
          <markerDef>RUT_BeastBulge</markerDef>
        </li>
      </elements>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
